{
 "verdict": "runtime",
 "cause": "PROMPT_CACHE_CHANGES_OUTPUT",
 "fix": {"action": "change_runtime_flag", "target": "prompt cache reuse (--no-cache-prompt / disable slot prompt caching)", "value": "disabled"},
 "rationale": "The timings show the first call evaluated the prompt fresh (cache_n=1, prompt_n=32) while the second call reused 28 cached tokens and only evaluated 5 (cache_n=28, prompt_n=5), and the outputs differ exactly along that boundary while subsequent cached calls agree with each other. At temperature 0 decoding is greedy, so the seed is irrelevant, and quantisation cannot explain a difference that appears only after a cache hit. Reusing the prompt cache changes how the prompt tokens are batched through the GPU kernels, which perturbs the logits slightly and flips an argmax, diverging the generation; disabling prompt cache reuse forces every call to run a full fresh prefill and makes the replies reproducible."
}

